import EpilineCaseLayout from '../../../layouts/EpilineCaseLayout.astro';
---
<EpilineCaseLayout title="Epiline CRM and booking case" description="How Epiline administrators manage a patient from new enquiry through WhatsApp, Kommo CRM, Altegio booking and follow-up." eyebrow="CRM / PATIENT JOURNEY" headline="From new lead" accent="to returning patient." intro="We designed the workflow from the clinic administrator’s point of view: a lead arrives, the patient gets an immediate response, the conversation continues, tasks are created, the appointment is booked — and the relationship does not disappear after the first visit." metrics={[{value:'KOMMO',label:'sales pipeline + administrator tasks'},{value:'ALTEGIO',label:'appointments + customer records'},{value:'WHATSAPP',label:'patient communication'}]}>

<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">THE REAL PROBLEM</span><div><h2>The difficult part starts<br/>after the lead arrives.</h2><p class="statement">A clinic can generate hundreds of enquiries and still lose patients between “I’m interested” and the treatment room.</p><p>The administrator has to respond quickly, understand what the patient needs, answer questions, follow up if they disappear, find a suitable time, book the visit and keep the relationship alive afterwards.</p><p>So we stopped looking at CRM as a database. We designed it as the clinic’s patient-conversion workflow.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="journey"><div class="shell"><div class="journey-head"><span class="eyebrow">ADMINISTRATOR VIEW / ONE PATIENT</span><h2>What the clinic actually sees.</h2><p>Below is a representative workflow showing how the connected system is designed to work. The interface is simplified to make the operational logic visible.</p></div>
<div class="timeline">
<div class="step"><div class="num">01</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">NEW ENQUIRY</span><h3>A lead arrives.</h3><p>The enquiry enters Kommo with its source and contact details. The administrator sees a new patient to work — not another form submission buried in email.</p></div><div class="ui lead"><div class="ui-top"><b>NEW LEAD</b><span>10:42</span></div><strong>Anna K.</strong><small>Laser hair removal · Riga</small><div class="tag">META ADS</div><div class="status">● New enquiry</div></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="num">02</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">IMMEDIATE RESPONSE</span><h3>The patient knows<br/>we received it.</h3><p>An immediate WhatsApp acknowledgement removes uncertainty while the administrator prepares a personal reply.</p></div><div class="phone"><div class="wa-head">WhatsApp · Epiline</div><div class="bubble incoming">Hi! I’d like to know more about laser hair removal.</div><div class="bubble outgoing">Hi Anna! Thank you for your enquiry — we’ve received it. Our administrator will help you shortly.</div><div class="bubble outgoing human">I can help now 👋 Is this your first laser hair removal treatment?</div><div class="bubble incoming">Yes. I’m interested in legs + bikini.</div></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="num">03</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">SALES / FOLLOW-UP</span><h3>No answer is not<br/>a lost lead.</h3><p>If the patient is not ready to book, the administrator creates the next action in Kommo: call tomorrow, send information, remind in a week or return to the conversation later.</p></div><div class="ui tasks"><div class="ui-top"><b>KOMMO / TASKS</b><span>ANNA K.</span></div><div class="task done"><i>✓</i><span>Reply in WhatsApp<small>Today · 10:45</small></span></div><div class="task"><i>○</i><span>Follow up<small>Tomorrow · 12:00</small></span></div><div class="task"><i>○</i><span>Send treatment preparation<small>After booking</small></span></div></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="num">04</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">BOOKING</span><h3>Conversation becomes<br/>an appointment.</h3><p>When the patient is ready, the administrator creates the appointment in Altegio while working with the lead. The sales context stays in Kommo; the actual clinic schedule lives in Altegio.</p></div><div class="ui booking"><div class="ui-top"><b>APPOINTMENT</b><span>ALTEGIO</span></div><div class="calendar"><span>SEP</span><strong>18</strong><small>FRIDAY</small></div><div class="booking-copy"><strong>Laser hair removal</strong><span>Anna K. · 14:30</span><span>Riga clinic</span><button>BOOKED ✓</button></div></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="num">05</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE VISIT</span><h3>Reduce the chance<br/>of a no-show.</h3><p>The workflow continues after booking: confirmation, preparation information and reminders can become part of the patient journey instead of relying on the administrator’s memory.</p></div><div class="phone reminder"><div class="wa-head">WhatsApp · Epiline</div><div class="bubble outgoing">Anna, your appointment is confirmed for Friday at 14:30 at our Riga clinic.</div><div class="bubble outgoing human">A quick reminder for tomorrow ✨ We’re looking forward to seeing you. Here’s what to know before your treatment.</div></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="num">06</div><div class="step-copy"><span class="eyebrow">AFTER THE FIRST VISIT</span><h3>The first visit is not<br/>the end of the funnel.</h3><p>The patient is now part of the clinic’s customer base. The team can continue the relationship: follow-up, next procedure, course reminders and repeat booking.</p></div><div class="ui lifecycle"><div class="ui-top"><b>PATIENT JOURNEY</b><span>ACTIVE</span></div><div class="life"><span>LEAD</span><b>→</b><span>BOOKED</span><b>→</b><span>VISITED</span><b>→</b><span class="active">FOLLOW-UP</span><b>→</b><span>REPEAT</span></div><div class="next"><small>NEXT ACTION</small><strong>Follow up after first treatment</strong><span>Task for administrator · +21 days</span></div></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="case-section accent"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">THE SYSTEM</span><h2>One patient journey.<br/>Different tools doing different jobs.</h2><div class="flow"><span>ADS / WEBSITE</span><b>→</b><span>KOMMO</span><b>→</b><span>WHATSAPP</span><b>→</b><span>FOLLOW-UP</span><b>→</b><span>ALTEGIO</span><b>→</b><span>VISIT</span><b>→</b><span>REPEAT</span></div><div class="data-list"><div class="data-row"><span>Kommo</span><span>Lead, sales stage, tasks, follow-ups, conversation context</span><strong>BEFORE BOOKING</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>WhatsApp</span><span>Fast patient communication and ongoing dialogue</span><strong>COMMUNICATION</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>Altegio</span><span>Appointment, schedule and existing customer record</span><strong>BOOKING</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>Administrator</span><span>One clear next action for every patient</span><strong>HUMAN LAYER</strong></div></div></div></section>

<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">WHY IT MATTERS</span><div><h2>Marketing should not stop<br/>at cost per lead.</h2><p class="statement">The acquisition system has to help the clinic convert interest into visits — and visits into relationships.</p><p>That means sales, follow-up, booking and retention are not separate from marketing. They are the operational continuation of it.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="case-section dark"><div class="shell two"><span class="eyebrow">THE RESULT</span><div><h2>Every lead has<br/>a next step.</h2><p class="statement">The administrator can see where the patient is, what has already happened and what needs to happen next.</p><p>Kommo manages the relationship before booking. WhatsApp keeps the conversation human. Altegio manages the appointment. Together they create a patient journey that can continue beyond the first visit.</p></div></div></section>
</EpilineCaseLayout>
